_Written by `claude-4` (claude, `sonnet`, medium) ([run](https://github.com/Jlore-Studios/JackiOh/actions/runs/44161280623)) before anyone built this. The night bot's builder starts from this section: edit it here to change the plan._

## Goal

A redeploy of the same commit with changed settings (a secret, a var) restarts a running game server. The Worker keeps a SHA-256 fingerprint of `containerEnv(settings)` in the `Server` object's storage. On the first request after a deploy, a server on the deployed commit whose stored fingerprint differs or is absent is retired on the existing path (SIGTERM, `RETIRE_WAIT_MS`, then destroy), and the request starts the new one. A server with the same fingerprint is left alone. A storage fault never restarts a live site. The edge README and `docs/architecture.md` say so, and "or wait for the next sleep" is removed. No ruling and no spec change: the Worker's operation is operational, not a spec matter.

## Files to touch

| File | | What changes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `apps/edge/src/routing.ts` | change | add `export async function settingsFingerprint(settings: ServerSettings): Promise<string>` after `containerEnv` |
| `apps/edge/src/index.ts` | change | add `SETTINGS_FINGERPRINT_KEY`, add `rememberSettings`, rework `retireOlderImage` and its doc comment |
| `apps/edge/src/routing.test.ts` | change | fingerprint tests |
| `apps/edge/src/index.test.ts` | change | storage helper, default storage for the Server helpers, three #3618 assertions, new describe |
| `apps/edge/README.md` | change | bullet "A deploy reaches the running server"; last sentence of "Settings" |
| `docs/architecture.md` | change | paragraph "A deploy restarts the server" (about line 265) |
| `docs/deploy-cloudflare.md` | change | one sentence on the "Change a secret" bullet (about line 354); the other redeploy steps stay as written |

Do not touch: `.github/`, `.harness/`, `.squishy/`, `bot/`, `.claude/`, `wrangler.jsonc`, any crate, `apps/web`, `spec/`. Add no ruling note, and cite no `R<n>` id in new names or comments, since `cargo jackioh spec check` cross-checks them.

## Steps

1. **`apps/edge/src/routing.ts`**: add after `containerEnv`:
   ```ts
   /** #4118: ...doc comment: lowercase hex SHA-256 of `containerEnv(settings)` as JSON with its names in order. Same settings in any key order give the same digest, and a change to any one changes it. A digest of secrets: never log or send it. */
   export async function settingsFingerprint(settings: ServerSettings): Promise<string> {
     const env = containerEnv(settings);
     const entries = Object.keys(env).sort().map((name) => [name, env[name]]);
     const digest = await crypto.subtle.digest("SHA-256", new TextEncoder().encode(JSON.stringify(entries)));
     return Array.from(new Uint8Array(digest), (byte) => byte.toString(16).padStart(2, "0")).join("");
   }
   ```
   Using `containerEnv` means the fingerprint covers every `SERVER_VARS` entry, every `SERVER_SECRETS` entry, `DEPLOYED_COMMIT`, `NODE_ENV` and `PORT`. An empty or unset setting hashes alike, as it reaches the container alike.

2. **`apps/edge/src/index.ts`**:
   - Add `settingsFingerprint` to the `./routing.ts` import list, in alphabetical position: `precompressedModule`, `settingsFingerprint`, then `type ServerSettings`.
   - Beside `TOLD_AT_KEY`, add:
     ```ts
     /** #4118: the key in the object's storage that holds the fingerprint (routing.ts `settingsFingerprint`) of the settings the container was last started with. Prefixed, like `TOLD_AT_KEY`; the value is never logged or sent. */
     export const SETTINGS_FINGERPRINT_KEY = "jackioh:server.settings:fingerprint";
     ```
   - Add this method next to `retireOlderImage`:
     ```ts
     /** #4118: keeps the fingerprint of the settings the next start takes. A write that fails is logged and costs at most one more restart at a later deploy. Never rejects. */
     private async rememberSettings(): Promise<void> {
       try {
         const fingerprint = await settingsFingerprint(this.env);
         await this.ctx.storage.put(SETTINGS_FINGERPRINT_KEY, fingerprint);
       } catch (error) {
         console.warn("server.settings_unwritten", error);
       }
     }
     ```
   - Rework `retireOlderImage`. Keep the health-fetch `try/catch` unchanged. Change the first line and what follows `running = ...`:
     ```ts
     if (!this.ctx.container?.running) {
       // Nothing to stop: the server the request starts next takes these settings, so remember them.
       await this.rememberSettings();
       return true;
     }
     // ...health fetch try/catch, unchanged...
     if (running === (this.env.DEPLOYED_COMMIT ?? null)) {
       try {
         const started = await this.ctx.storage.get<string>(SETTINGS_FINGERPRINT_KEY);
         if (started === (await settingsFingerprint(this.env))) return true;
       } catch (error) {
         // A storage fault is no reason to restart a live site; a later request asks again.
         console.warn("server.settings_unreadable", error);
         return false;
       }
       // Names no setting and carries no digest: the logs are not for secrets.
       console.warn("server.settings_changed");
     }
     try {
       await this.stop("SIGTERM");
       const deadline = Date.now() + RETIRE_WAIT_MS;
       while (this.ctx.container.running && Date.now() < deadline) {
         await new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, RETIRE_POLL_MS));
       }
       if (this.ctx.container.running) await this.destroy();
     } catch (error) {
       console.warn("server.retire_failed", error);
       return false;
     }
     await this.rememberSettings();
     return true;
     ```
     The old `return true` inside the retire `try` moves out, after it. A failed retire stores nothing. `rememberSettings` runs after both kinds of settled retire (older commit, changed settings), so a new object never restarts a server that was just started on the current settings.
   - Update `retireOlderImage`'s doc comment. Say it also stops a server on the deployed commit whose started-with settings differ from the Worker's (fingerprint in storage, absent counts as changed). Say it stores the fingerprint when it settles (no server, or retired). Say it resolves false also when the stored fingerprint cannot be read.

3. **`apps/edge/src/routing.test.ts`**: import `SERVER_SECRETS`, `SERVER_VARS` and `settingsFingerprint`. Add `describe("#4118 settingsFingerprint", …)` (tests below).

4. **`apps/edge/src/index.test.ts`**:
   - Add `SETTINGS_FINGERPRINT_KEY` to the `./index.ts` import and `settingsFingerprint` to the `./routing.ts` import.
   - After `COMMIT`, add:
     ```ts
     const SETTINGS = { DEPLOYED_COMMIT: COMMIT };
     /** The settings after a secret changed. */
     const CHANGED = { DEPLOYED_COMMIT: COMMIT, DEV_PROFILE_IDS: "profile-1" };
     const SECRET = "postgresql://postgres:hunter2@db.example.com/postgres";
     const FINGERPRINT = await settingsFingerprint(SETTINGS);

     /** An object's storage over a Map (two objects on one Map are a restart), holding `SETTINGS`' fingerprint unless given another Map. */
     function memoryStorage(entries = new Map<string, unknown>([[SETTINGS_FINGERPRINT_KEY, FINGERPRINT]])) {
       return {
         entries,
         get: vi.fn((key: string) => Promise.resolve(entries.get(key))),
         put: vi.fn((key: string, value: unknown) => { entries.set(key, value); return Promise.resolve(); }),
       };
     }
     /** Every argument a `console.warn` spy got, as text. */
     function logged(warn: { mock: { calls: unknown[][] } }): string {
       return JSON.stringify(warn.mock.calls.flat().map(String));
     }
     ```
   - `serverWith(running: boolean, storage = memoryStorage())`: ctx `{ container: { running }, waitUntil: vi.fn(), storage }`, env `SETTINGS`.
   - `serverWithCtx(ctx, env)`: pass `{ storage: memoryStorage(), ...(ctx as Record<string, unknown>) }` as the context, so a test's own `storage` wins and every existing call gets one.
   - Existing test `leaves a server on the deployed commit running`: create `const storage = memoryStorage()`, call `serverWith(true, storage)`, and add `expect(storage.put).not.toHaveBeenCalled()`.
   - #3618 describe (these now see the fingerprint write):
     - In `keeps when it told in the object's storage…`, replace `expect(handle.ctx.storage.put).toHaveBeenCalledOnce()` with `expect(handle.ctx.storage.put.mock.calls.filter(([key]) => key === TOLD_AT_KEY)).toHaveLength(1)`.
     - In `says nothing with no token and no email key, and keeps no time`, replace `expect(handle.ctx.storage.put).not.toHaveBeenCalled()` with `expect(handle.storage.has(TOLD_AT_KEY)).toBe(false)`. Keep the `get` assertion.
   - Add the new describe (tests below).

5. **Docs**:
   - `apps/edge/README.md`, bullet "A deploy reaches the running server": say a container keeps the image and the settings it started with. After the commit sentence, add that a server on the deployed commit is stopped the same way when the Worker's settings are not the ones it started with. The Worker keeps a SHA-256 fingerprint of the container's environment in the object's storage (`SETTINGS_FINGERPRINT_KEY`, never logged or sent) and logs `server.settings_changed`, naming no setting. A missing fingerprint counts as changed. An unreadable one leaves the server running and is asked about again (`server.settings_unreadable`). An unwritable one (`server.settings_unwritten`) costs at most one extra restart. Mention #4118.
   - Same README, "Settings": replace "so after changing one, deploy again (or wait for the next sleep)." with "so after changing one, deploy again: the first request after the deploy restarts a running server whose settings changed (above)."
   - `docs/architecture.md`, "A deploy restarts the server": add that it also stops a server on the deployed commit whose settings (the secrets among them) differ from the Worker's now, by a fingerprint kept in the object's storage (#4118), so a redeploy after a secret change takes effect.
   - `docs/deploy-cloudflare.md`, "Change a secret": after "…promote production with **redeploy**)", add "; the first request after it restarts a running server on the new settings."

## Tests

**`apps/edge/src/routing.test.ts`**, `describe("#4118 settingsFingerprint")`. For the sets below, `FULL = Object.fromEntries([...SERVER_VARS, ...SERVER_SECRETS, "DEPLOYED_COMMIT"].map((n) => [n, "v-" + n]))`.
- `is a 64-character lowercase hex SHA-256 of the sorted environment`: `await settingsFingerprint({})` matches `/^[0-9a-f]{64}$/u` and equals `c7c3f81364c145d758b33b174b0b165477042b321fe624abcdb8fb86a42faeb5`, which is the SHA-256 of `[["NODE_ENV","production"],["PORT","8080"]]`.
- `gives the same digest for the same settings in another key order`: `FULL` against `Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(FULL).reverse())`.
- `changes when any one setting changes`: for each name in `FULL`, `{ ...FULL, [name]: "changed" }` differs from `FULL`'s digest, and so does `FULL` with that name deleted. All the digests together (base plus changes) are distinct (`new Set(...).size`).
- `reads an empty setting as unset, and ignores what is not a server setting`: `{ CREATE_ISSUES_TOKEN: "" , SERVER: "a binding" }` as `ServerSettings` gives `settingsFingerprint({})`'s digest.

**`apps/edge/src/index.test.ts`**:
- Updated: `leaves a server on the deployed commit running`.
- New `describe("#4118 the settings check on the first request")` with `beforeEach(resetLibrary)`. Spy `console.warn` with `vi.spyOn(console, "warn").mockImplementation(() => undefined)`. A `container` is `{ running: true }` whose `stop` mock sets `running = false` and whose `startAndWaitForPorts` mock sets it back to true, as in the existing retire tests.
  1. `pins its storage key`: `SETTINGS_FINGERPRINT_KEY` is `"jackioh:server.settings:fingerprint"` and not `TOLD_AT_KEY`.
  2. `stops a server on the deployed commit whose settings changed, and the request starts the new one`:
     - Run `serverWithCtx({ container, storage }, CHANGED).fetch(request())` with `storage = memoryStorage()`. Expect `LISTENING`, `stop` called with `"SIGTERM"`, `destroy` not called, `startAndWaitForPorts` called once and after `stop` (`invocationCallOrder`).
     - The `server.settings_changed` calls equal `[["server.settings_changed"]]`.
     - `storage.entries.get(SETTINGS_FINGERPRINT_KEY)` equals `await settingsFingerprint(CHANGED)`.
  3. `waits RETIRE_WAIT_MS for it, then destroys it` (`vi.useFakeTimers()` in try/finally, `resetLibrary()` inside, and the stop mock a no-op as in `waits out a server on an older image…`): with `CHANGED`, advance 29_000 and expect `stop` called and `destroy` not. Advance 1_000 and expect `destroy` once. `await fetching`, then expect the changed fingerprint stored.
  4. `counts a missing fingerprint as changed`: `memoryStorage(new Map())`, env `SETTINGS`. Expect `stop` called with `"SIGTERM"` and `FINGERPRINT` stored afterwards.
  5. `stores the fingerprint when no server runs, and a new object on that storage leaves the server it started`:
     - Use `memoryStorage(new Map())` and a `{ running: false }` container whose start flips it on. After the first fetch, `FINGERPRINT` is stored and `containerFetch` was not called.
     - Fetch through a second `serverWithCtx({ container, storage }, SETTINGS)`. Expect `containerFetch` called once, `stop` not called, `startAndWaitForPorts` called once in all.
  6. `does not loop: after retiring for changed settings, a new object with the same settings leaves the server`: two objects on one `memoryStorage()`, both with `CHANGED`. `stop` called once and `startAndWaitForPorts` once in all.
  7. `remembers the settings after retiring an older commit too`:
     - `containerFetch` answers `x-deployed-commit: older` and the storage is `new Map()`. After the fetch, `FINGERPRINT` is stored.
     - Set `containerFetch` back to a COMMIT answer. A second object on that storage leaves the server: `stop` called once in all.
  8. `leaves the server running when the stored fingerprint cannot be read, and asks again after the retry interval` (fake timers in try/finally):
     - `storage.get.mockRejectedValueOnce(new Error("storage down"))`, env `{ ...CHANGED, DATABASE_URL: SECRET }`.
     - First fetch answers `LISTENING`, `stop` not called, and `warn` was called with `("server.settings_unreadable", expect.any(Error))`. `logged(warn)` contains neither `"hunter2"` nor `await settingsFingerprint(env)`.
     - `vi.advanceTimersByTime(IMAGE_CHECK_RETRY_MS)`, fetch again: `stop` called with `"SIGTERM"`.
  9. `still answers when the fingerprint cannot be written, with no server running`: `memoryStorage(new Map())`, `storage.put.mockRejectedValue(new Error("storage down"))`, a `{ running: false }` container, env `{ DEPLOYED_COMMIT: COMMIT, DATABASE_URL: SECRET }`. The answer is `LISTENING`, `startAndWaitForPorts` was called once, and `warn` was called with `("server.settings_unwritten", expect.any(Error))`. `logged(warn)` has no `"hunter2"` and no fingerprint.
  10. `still answers when the fingerprint cannot be written after a retire`: as 9, but a running container, `CHANGED` and `memoryStorage()` with a rejecting `put`. `stop` called, answer `LISTENING`, `server.settings_unwritten` logged.
  11. `stores nothing when the retire fails`: `library.stop.mockRejectedValue(new Error("refused"))`, `memoryStorage()`, `CHANGED`. The answer is `LISTENING`, `warn` was called with `("server.retire_failed", expect.any(Error))`, `storage.put` was not called, and the stored value is still `FINGERPRINT`.

**Commands** (if `node_modules` is missing, run `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` first):
```
